NAME
       mp3dec_init, mp3dec_decode_frame - MPEG audio decoding

SYNOPSIS
       #define MINIMP3_IMPLEMENTATION
       #define MINIMP3_NO_SIMD
       #include <minimp3.h>

       void mp3dec_init(mp3dec_t *dec);
       int  mp3dec_decode_frame(mp3dec_t *dec, const uint8_t *buf, int n,
                                short *pcm, mp3dec_frame_info_t *info);

DESCRIPTION
       Decodes one MPEG audio frame at a time. The decoder finds the
       next frame itself, so ID3 tags and other padding are skipped
       without help.

       The return value is the number of samples per channel, and
       info.frame_bytes says how far to advance; a zero there means no
       frame could be found and the loop should stop. info also carries
       the sample rate, the channel count and the bitrate.

       Define MINIMP3_NO_SIMD before including it: without that the
       header reaches for immintrin.h, which is not available here. No
       math library is needed.

EXAMPLE
              mp3dec_init(&dec);
              while (pos < len) {
                      int s = mp3dec_decode_frame(&dec, buf + pos,
                                                  len - pos, pcm, &info);
                      if (info.frame_bytes == 0) break;
                      pos += info.frame_bytes;
                      if (s > 0) play(pcm, s, info.channels);
              }

       mp3dec_f32_to_s16() converts a float buffer to the 16-bit
       samples the audio device expects.

SEE ALSO
       play(1), audio(2)
